! level 5 scenario 1 - vegetarian (no mince/tenderloin) - recipes are cupcakes (16$), croissants (16$), lasagna (12$), phyllo (12$), averaging 14$ (12.3$ if eggs/milk produced at home)
! legel 5 scenario 2 - veg-minmax (only phyllo/lasagna) - not possible to avoid more expensive cupcake/croissant recipes unless not stocking milk/eggs
! level 5 scenario 3 - omnivorous (adding meat recipes) - average cost 14.6$ if stocking all ingredients (13.4$ if produced at home)
! level 5 scenario 4 - omniminmax (only virgin egg pie) - only stock home-produced eggs, flower and virgin meat, fixes daily cost at 11$
! get virgin meat cheapest from Fogs (min slave auction market price is 20$ vs. cost of a healing balm is 8$)
! compare restaurant (8$) which is equivalent to S+ meal quality and club (included in A+ or higher cost of living) which is equivalent to A+ meal quality
! eating at the restaurant (which requires 5 merit to avoid spoiling) can save 3$ to 6.6$ per visit vs home cooking
! eating at the club is not an adequate substitute at this tier (will not maintain strength above A+) but can save 11$ to 14.6$ per day depending on the scenario vs home cooking
! eating at the pub is not an adequate substitute at this tier (will not maintain master strength above B+)

!Since the club is no longer S+ quality food, if the master is still hungry after eating there and if no one else cooks, he will cook for himself unless he ends the day with negative energy (at least one full red star). So it is still possible to "save" some money by eating at the club and overspending master energy (or not stocking [any/many/expensive] ingredients for the slave/assistant/master to auto-cook with). But if this is done, then unless regularly sparring top-tier opponents at the colosseum or hunting in the Fogs to compensate, master strength will eventually drop to A+. Can save 11$ to 14.6$ per day this way, which adds up (111$ / 146$ per decade). This is offset by medical and/or energy costs (sparring once a day is not enough).

!EXAMPLE
dynamic $fb_cycle, 'образец', ' [<<$food_quality[10]>>]', 'vegetables', 'grain', 'virgin_meat', 'spice'
